{number: 123}
{title: Father God Will I Know}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Father God, will I know you are gracious,
And I [F] know of your love for all [C] men,
Will I know that your love never changes,
There is [G7] hope for the ones yet in [C] sin.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
O [F] Lord fill me now with Thy [C] Spirit,
As I [G7] wait, fill me now Lord I [C] pray,
Till the [F] fire of your Spirit con-[C] sumes me,
Fill my [G7] heart in your own special [C] way.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
By the [C] power of the spirit within me,
Cleanse my [F] heart of the black stains of [C] sin,
Till my heart burns no more in its passion,
Till my [G7] longings are holy and [C] clean.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
Lord I [C] know that you died for the sinner,
That your [F] death gave new hope to all [C] men,
As in power from the tomb you ascended,
So in [G7] power come upon us a-[C] gain.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
Till the [C] earth is rolled up like a garment,
Till the [F] end of this age comes to [C] be;
Let us cease not our praise nor thanksgiving,
Let us [G7] thank Him for setting us [C] free.
{end_of_verse}
